# REQUIRES: python-api, hdf5
# A Python simulation and `mdir run` of one model in the deterministic mode
# give the same state bit for bit on the CPU: the dipeptide in water with
# SHAKE and SETTLE, from the velocities that both draw, double precision,
# CUTOFF electrostatics (scenario of Inputs/python_deterministic_run.py).
# With PME in mixed precision they differed after one step, since the forces
# that the steps carry took the type of the buffers of the host calls that
# the loop of steps reached, which the two programs place differently
# (#102, #105). They parted at the rounding of the sums of forces after about
# 20 steps (#121): the neighbor structures of the evaluation at the start
# carried into the steps of the simulation and of `mdir run` without
# checkpoints, while `mdir run` with checkpoints built them anew at the first
# step of its first segment, so the programs rebuilt at other steps. The
# evaluation at the start is now a segment of its own in every program
# (D[front-end-divergence]). Cases: N steps in one part against N steps with
# a checkpoint at the end; and 3 parts of 20 steps, and 5 of 7, against one
# run with a row at the end of each part, since the parts of a simulation
# continue one run in one activation (D215).
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: env MDIR_COMPILE_CACHE_DIR=%t/cache %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_deterministic_run.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide CPU mdir %t Double CUTOFF 1 19 20 21 50 20x3 7x5 | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: CPU Double CUTOFF 1: positions same velocities same forces same
# CHECK-NEXT: CPU Double CUTOFF 19: positions same velocities same forces same
# CHECK-NEXT: CPU Double CUTOFF 20: positions same velocities same forces same
# CHECK-NEXT: CPU Double CUTOFF 21: positions same velocities same forces same
# CHECK-NEXT: CPU Double CUTOFF 50: positions same velocities same forces same
# CHECK-NEXT: CPU Double CUTOFF 20x3: positions same velocities same forces same
# CHECK-NEXT: CPU Double CUTOFF 7x5: positions same velocities same forces same
